From 78254177fd963fee04f9e8a42bc603bac823dba2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nguyen Minh Tien <zizuzacker@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 09:01:33 +0700
Subject: [PATCH v2 0/2] iio: adc: Add Texas Instruments ADS1220 ADC
To: Jonathan Cameron <jic23@kernel.org>
Cc: linux-iio@vger.kernel.org,
    devicetree@vger.kernel.org,
    Rob Herring <robh@kernel.org>,
    Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzk+dt@kernel.org>,
    Conor Dooley <conor+dt@kernel.org>,
    David Lechner <dlechner@baylibre.com>,
    Nuno Sá <nuno.sa@analog.com>,
    Andy Shevchenko <andy@kernel.org>,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

This series adds support for the Texas Instruments ADS1220, a 24-bit,
2-kSPS, 4-channel delta-sigma ADC with an SPI (mode 1) interface, a
programmable gain amplifier (1 to 128), an internal 2.048V reference and
a dedicated DRDY data-ready output.

The driver supports:
 - single-ended and differential voltage channels described as
   device-tree child nodes;
 - per-channel programmable gain (via _scale) and data rate (via
   _sampling_frequency), with the matching *_available attributes;
 - the internal 2.048V reference, an external reference on REFP0/REFN0
   via a regulator, or the analog supply (AVDD) as a ratiometric
   reference for single-supply measurements;
 - single-shot conversions gated on the DRDY interrupt, or on a
   data-rate-derived delay when no interrupt is wired;
 - a DRDY-interrupt-driven triggered buffer for streaming;
 - runtime PM (power-down between conversions).

I tested this on a Lichee Pi Nano (Allwinner F1C100s) running Linux 7.0:
with a potentiometer on AIN0 (single-ended against AVSS, AVDD as the
reference), in_voltage0_raw tracks the wiper linearly across the full
0..3.3V range.

Thanks to everyone for the detailed v1 review.

Changes in v2:
dt-bindings:
 - Fix the invalid diff-channels YAML flow syntax: each pair now uses a
   proper block sequence of {const} items so dt_binding_check parses and
   validates two-element arrays (Conor, David, Sashiko).
 - Raise the channel limit from 7 to 12 to cover all four single-ended
   inputs and eight differential multiplexer combinations; the child
   node pattern and reg maximum are updated accordingly (Sashiko).
 - Document diff-channels polarity: the first cell is AINP (positive),
   the second AINN (negative), so e.g. <2 3> and <3 2> are both valid
   and differ only in polarity (Conor).
 - Note that DRDY must be wired to a dedicated host interrupt and cannot
   be shared with the SPI data lines (Jonathan).
 - Add the MAINTAINERS entry (with the binding file) in this patch and
   the driver file in patch 2 (Jonathan).

driver:
 - Make _scale consistent across read_raw, write_raw and read_avail by
   computing per-gain voltage scales from the reference at probe and
   exposing them as IIO_VAL_INT_PLUS_NANO, instead of gain reciprocals
   (Jonathan, Sashiko). This also removes the int overflow / divide-by-
   zero on the write path.
 - Negate the shorted-input reading returned for IIO_CHAN_INFO_OFFSET so
   user-space (raw + offset) * scale cancels the zero-scale error, and
   document why the shorted MUX setting is used (Jonathan, Sashiko).
 - Claim direct mode in write_raw so gain/data-rate changes cannot race
   an active buffer (Sashiko).
 - Resume the device around debugfs register access (Sashiko).
 - Stop continuous conversions on buffer postdisable so the device no
   longer asserts DRDY once streaming stops (Sashiko).
 - Drop the DMA-shared tx buffer: command and register writes now use
   spi_write_then_read() with on-stack buffers; only the DMA-safe
   conversion-result buffer remains, placed last and cacheline aligned,
   with the non-DMA scan buffer moved before it (Jonathan, Sashiko).
 - Only read the AVDD voltage when it is actually used as the reference,
   so a dummy regulator that cannot report a voltage no longer breaks
   probe (Jonathan, Sashiko).
 - Use a fully populated [AINP][AINN] mux table with U8_MAX markers and
   pass the input array to ads1220_map_mux() so the negative input is
   never read uninitialised (Jonathan, Andy).
 - ads1220_datarate_to_code() now returns -ENOENT for unknown rates and
   is reused for data-rate validation in write_raw (Andy).
 - Drop the redundant pm_runtime_mark_last_busy() calls (now implied by
   pm_runtime_put_autosuspend()), drop the unnecessary runtime resume
   callback and the bits_per_word assignment, use in_range() for the
   channel-count check, ARRAY_SIZE()/sizeof() where applicable, the
   USEC_PER_*/MSEC_PER_SEC time helpers, a static const channel template
   and a C99-named spi_device_id, and expand the RESET delay comment
   (Andy, Jonathan).
 - Add the driver to MAINTAINERS in this patch (Jonathan).

